Harry's like me, a traveling man.

00:24:39.780 --> 00:24:42.020
And the funny thing is, the more we travel,

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:45.590
the more we like to know that there's one special place somewhere

00:24:45.590 --> 00:24:46.910
that's all ours.

00:24:47.430 --> 00:24:50.000
A place that we can really call home.

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:51.490
Uh-oh.

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:53.050
Here comes you-know-who.

00:24:53.310 --> 00:24:54.850
Time for me to scrammy-voo.

00:24:55.890 --> 00:25:00.000
Can you believe some joker wanted to charge me $40

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:08.900
an hour plus parts to fix my machine hey why so gollum oh no Harry I won't let

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:13.940
schema take over your workshop and yes he can be greedy insulting and very

00:25:13.940 --> 00:25:21.020
insensitive we're talking about you so my job is to make sure that the station

00:25:21.020 --> 00:25:25.840
runs properly and that means the whole station so I have to figure out a way

00:25:25.840 --> 00:25:30.000
for us all to work well together you know I did not have

00:25:31.850 --> 00:25:32.850
I'm going to call headquarters.

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:36.460
Won't be necessary.

00:25:37.700 --> 00:25:42.000
B.C. Flanagan, chief roving inspector for the Indian Valley Railroad.

00:25:43.460 --> 00:25:45.260
I've been observing your station here.

00:25:46.010 --> 00:25:48.710
I must say I found it all very interesting.

00:25:51.130 --> 00:25:52.590
The name is Schemer.

00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:57.000
Vending magnet extraordinaire, cafe proprietor par excellence.

00:25:57.580 --> 00:26:00.000
Mr. Schemer, I like your jukebox.

00:26:00.510 --> 00:26:02.690
That claw machine is a classic.

00:26:02.690 --> 00:26:07.110
And you have some ambitious ideas about opening a cafe here.

00:26:07.110 --> 00:26:10.260
Now, let me see that letter from headquarters.

00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:12.260
Thank you.

00:26:12.260 --> 00:26:17.640
Mm-hmm.

00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:18.970
Oh and boy.

00:26:18.970 --> 00:26:19.970
What?

00:26:19.970 --> 00:26:21.970
That letter is hereby rescinded.

00:26:21.970 --> 00:26:25.640
That means it's no longer any good.

00:26:25.640 --> 00:26:29.200
And you're Mr. Cupper.

00:26:29.200 --> 00:26:29.640
Yes.

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:35.410
In my opinion, Mr. Cupper, the Indian Valley Railroad is lucky to have a man like you on

00:26:35.410 --> 00:26:37.080
his payroll.

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:38.040
Our apologies.

00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:42.010
Your workshop is yours for as long as you want it.

00:26:42.010 --> 00:26:43.010
Thank you!

00:26:43.010 --> 00:26:45.010
That's all I wanted to hear!

00:26:45.010 --> 00:26:50.840
As for you, Mr. Schemer, like I said, you have a lot of ambitious ideas.

00:26:50.840 --> 00:26:51.780
And that's fine.

00:26:51.780 --> 00:26:56.920
You need a bit more modesty and a lot more sense.

00:26:56.920 --> 00:26:59.040
Get over here, Schemer!

00:26:59.040 --> 00:27:00.000
Why?

00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:04.930
what well how do you expect me to fix your machine if my tools are locked up

00:27:04.930 --> 00:27:12.120
behind this door oh hey yeah hey you know what Harry I think that I learned a

00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:16.020
little something from this misunderstanding that we had I really

00:27:16.020 --> 00:27:19.800
don't think that we need a snack bar around here what we need is a guy who

00:27:19.800 --> 00:27:26.900
can fix arcade machines yeah and I mean that thank you mr. Flanagan what we

00:27:26.900 --> 00:27:30.000
would have done without Harry and his workshop you can thank

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:35.270
yourself miss joe the things you've been saying make a lot of sense it's good you

00:27:35.270 --> 00:27:47.340
held your ground and stood up for what you believe in reach for the speed reach

00:27:47.340 --> 00:27:59.280
for the whistle go where the rail may run reach for the words reach for the story follow the rainbow sun

00:28:00.860 --> 00:28:04.270
To a shining time station

00:28:04.270 --> 00:28:07.200
Where dreams can come true

00:28:07.200 --> 00:28:11.260
Waiting there for you

00:28:11.260 --> 00:28:13.310
So much to see

00:28:13.310 --> 00:28:15.300
So far to travel

00:28:15.300 --> 00:28:18.430
So much to learn to know

00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:20.900
Friends by your side

00:28:20.900 --> 00:28:23.000
Hopes to hold on to

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:26.600
Who knows how far you'll go

00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:30.000
To a shining time station

00:28:30.990 --> 00:28:32.990
Where dreams can come true

00:28:32.990 --> 00:28:36.940
Your own imagination

00:28:36.940 --> 00:28:39.730
Waiting there for you
